# Line endings that must not depend on who checked the file out.
#
# A shell script with CRLF fails on macOS and Linux ("bad interpreter"), and a
# batch file with LF misparses labels and blocks on Windows. Git's autocrlf
# would otherwise rewrite both to whatever the local machine prefers.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
